":"Article 27"}},"value":1.25}],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":[],"accessibilities":{"list":[252,255,256,257,259,261,263,265],"translations":{"fr":["Accessible aux personnes ayant des difficult\u00e9s de compr\u00e9hension","Accessible","Am\u00e9nagements pour les personnes aveugles et malvoyantes","Am\u00e9nagements pour personnes sourdes et malentendantes","Chien d'assistance","Parking accessible","Accessible aux pi\u00e9tons appareill\u00e9s","WC adapt\u00e9"],"nl":["Toegankelijk voor mensen met een verstandelijke beperking","Toegankelijk","Voorzieningen voor blinde en slechtziende personen","Voorzieningen voor dove en slechthorende personen","Assistentiehonden","Toegankelijke parking","Toegankelijk voor voetgangers met hulpmiddelen","Aangepast toilet"],"en":["Accessible to people with intellectual disabilities","Accessible","Facilities for blind and partially-sighted persons","Facilities for deaf and hearing-impaired people","Assistance dogs","Accessible parking","Accessible to pedestrians with mobility aids","Adapted toilet"]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2022-06-10T01:06:07+02:00","published_at":"2022-01-27T08:04:00+01:00","backoffice_id":246258,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"expo","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.1552001266103},{"id":533599,"date_start":"2022-06-02","date_end":"2022-07-22","date_next":"2022-06-10","accept_article27":true,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":true,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition"}},"others":{"list":[36,46],"translations":{"fr":["Mus\u00e9es et art centers","Pluridisciplinaire"],"nl":["Musea en kunstcentra","Multidisciplinair"],"en":["Museums and art centers","Multidisciplinary"]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["nl","fr","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica","shortdescr":"Avec l\u2019exposition \"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica\", les artistes veulent nous raconter comment leur regard c\u00f4toie leur propre histoire de migration. Tous les trois vivent \u00e0 Bruxelles et, bien qu\u2019ils utilisent des formes et des techniques diff\u00e9rentes (peinture, gravure et performance), il en ressort une unit\u00e9 \u00e0 travers leur inspiration \"Ecuatorianismos\".","longdescr":"Trois regards artistiques \u00e9quatoriens : Alejandra Bed\u00f3n, Marco Campa\u00f1a Salgado et Diana Valarezo. Alejandra Bed\u00f3n pr\u00e9sente une s\u00e9rie de gravures avec une nouvelle perspective sur l\u2019art botanique. On sent la fascination pour le germe de la vie dans ses compositions rythm\u00e9es et harmonieuses. Marco Campa\u00f1a Salgado nous pr\u00e9sente des couleurs vives, ses peintures refl\u00e9tant une fusion magique entre l\u2019ancien et le contemporain et nous tenant un miroir. Et Diana Valarezo pr\u00e9sente \u00e0 cette occasion la performance \"Rasgar las vestiduras\", dans laquelle elle utilise la broderie pour raconter son histoire de migration et \u00e0 la suite l\u2019histoire universelle de migration.\r\n\r\nCette exposition est une collaboration avec\r\nEmbajada de Espa\u00f1a en B\u00e9lgica\r\nMisi\u00f3n del Ecuador ante la Uni\u00f3n Europea","performers":"Alejandra Bed\u00f3n (engravings), Marco Campa\u00f1a Salgado (paintings), Diana Valarezo (broderie).","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","email":"museum@foyer.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/fr\/detail\/id\/533599.html"},"nl":{"name":"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica","shortdescr":"Met de tentoonstelling \"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica\" willen de kunstenaars ons vertellen hoe hun blik samengaat men hun eigen migratieverhaal. Ze wonen alle drie in Brussel en hoewel ze verschillende vormen en technieken gebruiken (schilderkunst, gravure en performance) is er \u00e9\u00e9nheid door de inspiratiebron \u201cEcuatorianismos\u201d.","longdescr":"Drie Ecuadoraanse artistieke blikken: Alejandra Bed\u00f3n, Marco Campa\u00f1a Salgado en Diana Valarezo. Alejandra Bed\u00f3n presenteert een serie gravures met een nieuwe kijk op botanische kunst. We voelen de fascinatie voor de levenskiem in haar ritmische en harmonieuze composities. Marco Campa\u00f1a Salgado brengt ons levendige kleuren, zijn schilderwerken weerspiegelen een magische versmelting tussen het oude en het hedendaagse en houden ons een spiegel voor. En Diana Valarezo presenteert bij deze gelegenheid de performance \u201cRasgar las vestiduras\u201d, waarbij ze via borduurwerk haar en zo ook het universele migratieverhaal brengt.\r\n\r\nDeze tentoonstelling is een samenwerking met\r\nEmbajada de Espa\u00f1a en B\u00e9lgica\r\nMisi\u00f3n del Ecuador ante la Uni\u00f3n Europea","performers":"Alejandra Bed\u00f3n (gravures), Marco Campa\u00f1a Salgado (schilderwerken), Diana Valarezo (borduurwerk).","boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 609 55 61","agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/nl\/detail\/id\/533599.html"},"en":{"name":"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica","shortdescr":"With the exhibition \"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica\", the artists want to tell us how their vision merges with their own migration story. All three live in Brussels and, although they use different forms and techniques (painting, engraving and performance), there is unity through the inspiration of \"Ecuatorianismos\".","longdescr":"Three Ecuadorian artistic eyes: Alejandra Bed\u00f3n, Marco Campa\u00f1a Salgado and Diana Valarezo. Alejandra Bed\u00f3n presents a series of engravings with a new perspective on botanical art. We feel the fascination for the germ of life in her rhythmic and harmonious compositions. Marco Campa\u00f1a Salgado brings us vivid colours, his paintings reflecting a magical fusion between the ancient and the contemporary and holding up a mirror to us. And Diana Valarezo on this occasion presents the performance \"Rasgar las vestiduras\", in which she uses embroidery to tell the universal story of migration.\r\n\r\nThis exhibition is a collaboration with\r\nEmbajada de Espa\u00f1a en B\u00e9lgica\r\nMisi\u00f3n del Ecuador ante la Uni\u00f3n Europea","performers":"Alejandra Bed\u00f3n (gravures), Marco Campa\u00f1a Salgado (peintures), Diana Valarezo (embroidery).","boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/en\/detail\/id\/533599.html"},"de":{"name":"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/de\/detail\/id\/533599.html"},"it":{"name":"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/it\/detail\/id\/533599.html"},"sp":{"name":"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/sp\/detail\/id\/533599.html"},"pt":{"name":"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/pt\/detail\/id\/533599.html"},"cn":{"name":"Ecuatorianismos en B\u00e9lgica","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/cn\/detail\/id\/533599.html"}},"place":{"id":274307,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","address_line1":"rue des ateliers, 17","address_line2":"1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","description_web":"Aujourd'hui, plus de 180 nationalite\u0301s vivent ensemble a\u0300 Bruxelles. Le MigratieMuseumMigration raconte l\u2019histoire de la premie\u0300re ge\u0301ne\u0301ration de travailleurs immigre\u0301s invite\u0301s, des premiers arrivants au Petit Cha\u0302teau, des expatrie\u0301s, des re\u0301fugie\u0301s de guerre, des Europe\u0301ens qui se sont de\u0301place\u0301s librement au sein de l\u2019UE et de tous les autres. C\u2019est un muse\u0301e chaleureux ou\u0300 les visiteurs peuvent de\u0301couvrir la ville et la vie des autres a\u0300 travers des souvenirs, mais aussi, et avant tout, un lieu accueillant pour y partager sa propre histoire.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"Werkhuizenstraat","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Sint-Jans-Molenbeek","address_line1":"Werkhuizenstraat, 17","address_line2":"1080 Sint-Jans-Molenbeek","description_web":"Vandaag de dag wonen meer dan 180 nationaliteiten samen in Brussel. Het MigratieMuseumMigration geeft de verhalen van de eerste generatiegastarbeiders, van de vroegste bewoners van het Klein Kasteeltje, van de expats, de oorlogsvluchtelingen, de Europeanen die zich vrij bewegen binnen de EU en vele anderen een permanente thuis. Het is een warme omgeving waar bezoekers via herinneringen en kunst op ontdekking gaan in Brussel en in het leven van anderen.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","address_line1":"rue des ateliers, 17","address_line2":"1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","description_web":"Today, more than 180 nationalities live together in Brussels. The MigratieMuseumMigration gives a permanent home to the stories of the first generation of guest workers, of the earliest inhabitants of the Petit-Cha\u0302teau, of the expats, the war refugees, the Europeans who move freely within the EU and many others. It is a warm environment where visitors can discover Brussels and the lives of others through memories and souvenirs. Above all, it is a museum with plenty of room to share your own story.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","address_line1":"rue des ateliers, 17","address_line2":"1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be",