ull,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des Egouts de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des Egouts de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des Egouts de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des Egouts de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":[],"zones":{"list":[19],"translations":{"fr":["Centre"],"nl":["Centrum"],"en":["Centre"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":36382,"location":{"lat":50.84483547,"lon":4.33883369},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-06-05T01:06:51+02:00","published_at":"2021-03-13T17:56:01+01:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":false,"is_in_vb_export":false,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":231869,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts - Mus\u00e9es de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Au premier abord, on n\u2019y aurait pas pens\u00e9\u2026 Aller visiter les \u00e9gouts d\u2019une grande ville ? Mais en y r\u00e9fl\u00e9chissant un court instant, on per\u00e7oit vite l\u2019int\u00e9r\u00eat et les apprentissages potentiels ! Cet endroit qu\u2019aujourd\u2019hui on n\u2019imagine pas autrement qu\u2019enfoui\u2026 n\u2019a pas toujours exist\u00e9 sous cette forme, loin s\u2019en faut !\r\nC\u2019est au 17e si\u00e8cle que se met en place \u00e0 Bruxelles le premier r\u00e9seau d\u2019\u00e9gouts ; toutefois celui-ci reste \u00e9l\u00e9mentaire et bon nombre de d\u00e9chets terminent encore leur itin\u00e9raire dans le cours d\u2019eau bruxellois, la Senne. Celle-ci charrie d\u00e9tritus et charognes, et d\u00e9borde r\u00e9guli\u00e8rement en temps de pluie, ou s\u2019ass\u00e8che en \u00e9t\u00e9, laissant s\u2019\u00e9chapper des odeurs peu subtiles\u2026\r\nUn grand plan d\u2019assainissement est ex\u00e9cut\u00e9 dans la seconde moiti\u00e9 du 19e si\u00e8cle. On d\u00e9cide de vo\u00fbter la Senne et d\u2019\u00e9tablir de larges boulevards \u00e0 la place des ruelles insalubres. Durant l\u2019entre-deux-guerres, une deuxi\u00e8me entreprise de d\u00e9tournement et de vo\u00fbtement du cours d\u2019eau viendra renforcer l\u2019efficacit\u00e9 des premiers travaux.\r\nProgressivement, le r\u00e9seau des \u00e9gouts va se perfectionner et s\u2019agrandir : comptant 45 km en 1847, on d\u00e9nombre actuellement 350 km de d\u00e9dales souterrains, qui recueillent conjointement les eaux pluviales et les eaux us\u00e9es provenant de l\u2019activit\u00e9 humaine. \r\nOuvert en 1988 pour r\u00e9pondre \u00e0 une demande croissante, le mus\u00e9e propose \u00e0 cette \u00e9poque des visites assur\u00e9es par le personnel du Service des Egouts lui-m\u00eame.\r\nAper\u00e7u de ce r\u00e9seau, explications sur son histoire et le travail des hommes qui l\u2019entretiennent, cycle de l\u2019eau, etc. : ce sont l\u00e0 quelques-unes des th\u00e9matiques qui vous y attendent ! Notez que l\u2019entr\u00e9e du mus\u00e9e si\u00e8ge dans un des deux \u00ab pavillons d\u2019octroi \u00bb, b\u00e2timents qui mat\u00e9rialisent la perception de la taxe sur tous les biens entrant dans la Ville au 19e si\u00e8cle.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Riolenmuseum - Musea van de stad Brussel","address_street_name":"Octrooipaviljoen, Anderlechtsepoort","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.riolenmuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Octrooipaviljoen, Anderlechtsepoort","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Zet eens een bezoek aan de Brusselse riolen en het Riolenmuseum op het programma van een uitstap in Brussel! Apart, ongewoon en onverwacht, maar vooral interessant en allesbehalve saai is zo\u2019n afdaling in ondergronds Brussel, begeleid door ervaren stadsgidsen of (voormalige) rioolwerkers.\r\nRiolen zijn levensnoodzakelijk geworden voor onze manier van leven, vandaar dat we ons maar moeilijk kunnen voorstellen hoe het eraan toeging toen ze nog niet bestonden. Een bezoek aan het Riolenmuseum (en een echte riool!) is dan ook verrassend, ongewoon en ongemeen boeiend.\r\nIn de 17de eeuw werd in Brussel een eerste riolennet in gebruik genomen. Dat bleef nog erg beperkt en het overgrote deel van het afvalwater vond nog altijd zijn weg naar die ene Brusselse rivier, de Zenne. Die voerde dan ook een smurrie van afval, viezigheid en zelfs dierenkadavers de hele stad door. Als de Zenne bij overvloedige regen overstroomde of in volle zomer opdroogde in de zomer, zorgde dat natuurlijk voor weinig aangename geurtjes...\r\nGedeeltelijk omwille van die overlast besloot de overheid in de tweede helft van de 19de eeuw om een overwelving aan te brengen boven de Zenne en grote boulevards aan te leggen in plaats van de vieze en slordige steegjes. Later werd tussen de twee Wereldoorlogen nog een tweede keer ingegrepen: een deel van de Zenne werd verlegd en er werden nog meer overwelvingen aangebracht. \r\nLangzamerhand verbeterde en vergrootte het riolennet, van 45 km in 1847 naar de huidige 350 km riool, die zowel afval- als regenwater afvoert. \r\nNaast een bezoek aan de riolen zelf levert dit in1988 opgerichte museum een schat aan boeiende en interessante informatie op over alle aspecten van riolen, rioolwater en de mensen die ze \u2013 vaak in gevaarlijke en altijd in onaangename omstandigheden - onderhouden. Leuk: de ingang van het museum is gehuisvest in een van de twee octrooipaviljoenen aan de Anderlechtse Poort, waar vroeger tol werd geheven op goederen die in de stad werden binnengebracht.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Sewers Museum - Museums of the City of Brussels","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.sewermuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Why not visit the Brussels sewers and the Sewers museum during your next excursion in Brussels. A visit of Brussels' sewerage network - led by experienced guides or ex-workers - is extraordinary, full of surprises, but above all fascinating. The sewers have become vital to our way of life, so much so that it's hard to imagine what it was like before they existed. A visit of the Sewers Museum (and a real sewer!) is therefore an amazing, unusual and thrilling experience.\r\nBrussels' first sewerage network came into use in the 17th century, but they were very limited and a large part of the city's waste still found its way into the river Senne. The river carried waste and carrion and regularly overflowed, or dried out in the summer, leaving behind less-than-pleasant smells.\r\nIt was partially due to this, that the government in the second half of the 19th century decided to completely transform the Senne and its neighbouring streets by building great boulevards to cover the insalubrious area. Between the two world wars a second transformation: a portion of the Senne was diverted and then covered over. The sewerage network improved and grew over the years, going from 45 km in 1847 to the 350 km that we have today.\r\nOpened in 1988, the museum used to offer guided tours with sewer staff. Tours present you with an overview of the network, a presentation of its history and the work of the people who maintain it and much more. The entrance to the museum is housed in one of the toll pavilions that used to collect taxes on goods that entered the city.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Kanalisationsmuseum (Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts)","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das Kanalisationsmuseum f\u00fchrt Sie hinab in die Unterwelten der Br\u00fcsseler Kanalisation. Entdecken Sie die Geheimnisse des faszinierenden, 400 Kilometer langen Labyrinths, das sich unter dem Br\u00fcsseler Stadtgebiet auftut. Tausende Kubikmeter Wasser flie\u00dfen t\u00e4glich durch die Br\u00fcsseler Abwasserkanalisation. Was mit ihnen geschieht, welche Wege sie nehmen, erfahren Sie im Kanalisationsmuseum - ein Museum mit vielen interessanten Details f\u00fcr Gro\u00df und Klein: Geschichtliches, Technisches und Am\u00fcsantes.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts - Mus\u00e9es de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Museo del Alcantarillado (Mus\u00e9e des Egouts)","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"En un primer momento, a uno no se le pasar\u00eda por la cabeza... \u00bfIr a visitar las alcantarillas de una gran ciudad? Pero si te paras a pensarlo, \u00a1ver\u00e1s r\u00e1pidamente el potencial de aprendizaje y el inter\u00e9s! Este lugar que, actualmente, solo nos imaginamos bajo tierra no siempre lo ha estado, ni mucho menos. En el siglo XVII se cre\u00f3 el primer sistema de alcantarillado en Bruselas; sin embargo, segu\u00eda siendo b\u00e1sico y muchos residuos terminaban su recorrido en el r\u00edo de la ciudad, el Senne. Este r\u00edo, que llevaba basura y carro\u00f1a, se sol\u00eda desbordar normalmente en \u00e9poca de lluvias, o se secaba en verano, lo que hac\u00eda que desprendiera olores desagradables...\r\nEn la segunda mitad del siglo XIX se puso en marcha un importante plan de saneamiento.\r\nSe decidi\u00f3 recubrir el Senne y crear amplios bulevares en lugar de callejones insalubres. Durante el per\u00edodo de entreguerras, unas segundas obras de recubrimiento y desv\u00edo del agua reforzaron las primeras. Gradualmente, el sistema de alcantarillado se mejor\u00f3 y ampli\u00f3: de 45 km en 1847, actualmente hay 350 km de laberintos subterr\u00e1neos, que recogen conjuntamente el agua de lluvia y las aguas residuales de la ciudad. El museo se inaugur\u00f3 en 1988 como respuesta a una demanda creciente y ofrece visitas realizadas por el propio personal del Servicio de Alcantarillado. Gracias a este museo podr\u00e1s disfrutar de una perspectiva general de esta red, explicaciones sobre su historia y sobre la labor que desempe\u00f1an sus trabajadores, informaci\u00f3n sobre el ciclo hidrol\u00f3gico, etc. Cabe destacar que la entrada al museo se encuentra en uno de los dos Pavillons d\u2019octroi, los edificios donde se recaudaban los impuestos de todas las mercanc\u00edas que entraban en la ciudad en el siglo XIX.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts - Mus\u00e9es de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts - Mus\u00e9es de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":989,"location":{"lat":50.82833819,"lon":4.31090786},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-06-05T01:06:51+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:58+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels.imgix.net\/497c8f280775147feabe55eaef62297958f3821f.jpg","width":2362,"height":3543,"ratio":0.67,"translations":{"fr":{"title":"Premier samedi du mois","copyright":"E.Danhier"},"nl":{"title":"Premier samedi du mois","copyright":"E.Danhier"},"en":{"title":"Premier samedi du mois","copyright":"E.Danhier"}}},{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels.imgix.net\/eafca1cd044f1a1116f01afe23e71bc8175599fe.jpg","width":950,"height":633,"ratio":1.5,"translations":{"fr":{"title":"Premier samedi du mois","copyright":"E.Danhier"},"nl":{"title":"Premier samedi du mois","copyright":"E.Danhier"},"en":{"title":"Premier samedi du mois","copyright":"E.Danhier"}}}],"dates":[{"day":"2021-10-02","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2021-11-06","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2021-12-04","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-01-01","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-02-05","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-03-05","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-04-02","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-05-07","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-06-04","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-07-02","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-08-06","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-09-03","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-10-01","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-11-05","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2022-12-03","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"},{"day":"2023-01-07","doors":null,"start":"10:00:00","end":"17:00:00"}],"recurring":[{"day":"saturday","occurences":{"is_first":true,"is_second":false,"is_third":false,"is_fourth":false,"is_last":false},"time_start":"10:00:00","time_end":"17:00:00","translations":{"fr":"Ouvert le premier samedi du mois de 10:00 \u00e0 17:00","nl":"Open op de eerste zaterdag van de maand van 10:00 tot 17:00","en":"Open the first saturday of the month from 10:00 to 17:00"}}],"prices":[{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Normal"},"nl":{"name":"Normaal"},"en":{"name":"Normal"}},"value":0},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Enfants"},"nl":{"name":"Kinderen"},"en":{"name":"Children"}},"value":0}],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":[],"accessibilities":[],"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2022-06-05T01:06:51+02:00","published_at":"2021-10-11T16:30:18+02:00","backoffice_id":240858,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"tour","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.12926263449024},{"id":518572,"date_start":"2021-10-02","date_end":"2022-12-03","date_next":"2022-07-02","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":102,"translations":{"fr":"Visites Guid\u00e9es","nl":"Begeleide rondleidingen","en":"Guided tours"}},"others":{"list":[105],"translations":{"fr":["Gastronomie"],"nl":["Gastronomie"],"en":["Gastronomy"]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"DISCOVER & TASTE Coffee Tour - Downtown Kanaal","shortdescr":"Le caf\u00e9 de sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9 est en plein d\u00e9veloppement \u00e0 Bruxelles, avec l'\u00e9mergence de nouveaux caf\u00e9s et d'initiatives comme la Brussels Coffee Week, mais aussi gr\u00e2ce \u00e0 l\u2019impl\u00e9mentation de grains de qualit\u00e9 dans de plus en plus de lieux HoReCa, \u00e9piceries etc.","longdescr":"LES COFFEE TOURS\r\nLe caf\u00e9 de sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9 est en plein d\u00e9veloppement \u00e0 Bruxelles, avec l'\u00e9mergence de nouveaux caf\u00e9s et d'initiatives comme la Brussels Coffee Week, mais aussi gr\u00e2ce \u00e0 l\u2019impl\u00e9mentation de grains de qualit\u00e9 dans de plus en plus de lieux HoReCa, \u00e9piceries etc. Le caf\u00e9 de sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9 reste malgr\u00e9 tout encore bien trop m\u00e9connu, il est temps d'explorer ce que la capitale de l'Europe a \u00e0 offrir. Ces explorations caf\u00e9\u00efn\u00e9es de la ville sont aussi inhabituelles, amusantes qu\u2019instructives et correspondent \u00e0 un cours de base complet sur le caf\u00e9, le fun et la marche en plus.\r\n\r\nPOUR QUI\r\nLes Brussels Coffee Tours s'adressent \u00e0 tout le monde, avec un focus sur l\u2019exp\u00e9rience consommateur\/coffee lovers d\u00e9sireu.x.ses de mieux comprendre leur boisson favorite. Il convient \u00e9galement aux professionnel.le.s de l\u2019HoReCa qui encore souvent ignorent ce qu\u2019est le caf\u00e9 de sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9, les aidant ainsi \u00e0 comprendre le parent pauvre de leur secteur mais aussi \u00e0 mieux appr\u00e9hender l\u2019exp\u00e9rience client li\u00e9e au caf\u00e9. Je suis l\u00e0 pour aider et esp\u00e8re combler le foss\u00e9 entre les amateurs et les professionnels. Aucun pr\u00e9requis n'est n\u00e9cessaire \u00e0 ce tour. Les buveuses et buveurs de th\u00e9 appr\u00e9cient grandement ce tour, m\u00eame quand ils pensent ne pas aimer le caf\u00e9 ;)\r\n\r\nOBJECTIF\r\nLe but des Brussels Coffee Tours est de faire d\u00e9couvrir les lieux innovants lorsqu\u2019il est question de caf\u00e9 de sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9, mais aussi de d\u00e9couvrir et comprendre comment consommer \/ go\u00fbter le caf\u00e9 sur base de crit\u00e8res de qualit\u00e9 objectifs. Comprendre la cha\u00eene de production du champ \u00e0 la tasse, la diff\u00e9rence entre caf\u00e9 de sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9 et caf\u00e9 de commodit\u00e9 et apprendre \u00e0 mieux acheter son caf\u00e9 sont \u00e9galement au c\u0153ur des objectifs des Coffee Tours.\r\n\r\nDISCOVER & TASTE, UN TOUR P\u00c9DAGOGIQUE ! - EDITION DOWNTOWN KANAAL\r\nLors des Brussels Coffee Tours - Discover and Taste - , nous d\u00e9ambulons dans diff\u00e9rents quartiers de Bruxelles, en fonction de l\u2019\u00e9dition, car voyager autour du caf\u00e9 de sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9 est toujours une excellente id\u00e9e pour d\u00e9couvrir les tendances locales. Nous stimulerons vos papilles en go\u00fbtant un espresso, une boisson lact\u00e9e, mais aussi des m\u00e9thodes filtre et parfois m\u00eame des infusions \u00e0 froid, azot\u00e9es ou non, le tout \u00e0 mes frais. Vous ne payez pas d'extra pour vos boissons.\r\n\r\nLors de cette \u00e9dition DOWNTOWN KANAAL, nous visitons 4 \u00e0 5 lieux dans les magnifiques quartiers Monnaie\/Dansaert, avec mini d\u00e9gustation de diff\u00e9rentes fermentations \u00e0 la clef. Nous vous sensibiliserons aux m\u00e9tiers du caf\u00e9 et aborderons diff\u00e9rents sujets tels que : les diff\u00e9rences de philosophies et les nouvelles vagues, les m\u00e9thodes de pr\u00e9paration, les habitudes de consommation, le m\u00e9tier de barista, la science derri\u00e8re le lait, le sucre, le go\u00fbt, la qualit\u00e9, le caf\u00e9 de sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9, les labels, les styles de torr\u00e9faction, les recettes etc\u2026 mais aussi les informations \u00e0 d\u00e9crypter sur les sachets de caf\u00e9 afin de mieux acheter et d\u00e9jouer le marketing global.\r\n\r\nGOOD TO KNOW\r\nLes tours se passent toujours en ext\u00e9rieur. Nous marchons d'un endroit \u00e0 l'autre et jetons un \u0153il aux lieux, mais les groupes \u00e9tant grands par rapport \u00e0 la capacit\u00e9 des lieux, nous ne consommons pas assis \u00e0 l\u2019int\u00e9rieur. Il est pr\u00e9f\u00e9rable de se munir de chaussures confortables, de v\u00eatements CHAUDS en hiver (mieux vaut trop de couches que pas assez !!) et un parapluie en cas de pluie. De l\u2019eau est toujours recommand\u00e9e \u00e9galement. Masque et gel en temps de Covid. \r\n\r\nPetit d\u00e9jeunez avant la visite car nous n'avons pas le temps de manger lors des tours. Pssst, rejoins-nous : INSTA @ok_coffee_tips\r\n\r\nVOTRE GUIDE\r\nThomas Wyngaard est fondateur de OK Coffee et un des rares experts en Caf\u00e9 de Sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9 en Belgique francophone. Il est consultant ind\u00e9pendant, enseignant (certifi\u00e9 par la Specialty Coffee Association de janvier 2018 \u00e0 avril 2021), tour-ist et broadcaster. Apr\u00e8s avoir \u00e9t\u00e9 form\u00e9 en France, en Pologne et en Estonie, il fait ses armes chez les meilleurs en Belgique, pour ensuite migrer pendant presque 2 ans \u00e0 New York o\u00f9 il a offici\u00e9 comme conseiller et formateur. Au-del\u00e0 de la formation sur les m\u00e9tiers du caf\u00e9, il collabore avec des torr\u00e9facteurs belges engag\u00e9s sur la reconnaissance du caf\u00e9 de sp\u00e9cialit\u00e9, \u0153uvrant ainsi \u00e0 un monde meilleur \u201cone bean at a time\u201d.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.okcoffee.tips","email":"thomas@okcoffee.tips","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/fr\/detail\/id\/518572.html"},"nl":{"name":"DISCOVER & TASTE Coffee Tour - Downtown Kanaal","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/nl\/detail\/id\/518572.html"},"en":{"name":"DISCOVER & TASTE Coffee Tour - Downtown Kanaal","shortdescr":"Be ready to discover and taste the new waves of coffee during this 4 hours tour in the Downtown Kanaal Brussels area. Hosted in FR & EN.","longdescr":"THE COFFEE TOURS\r\nSpecialty coffee is booming in Brussels, with the emergence of new coffee shops and initiatives like the Brussels Coffee Week, but also thanks to the implementation of quality beans in more and more HoReCa places, grocery stores etc. However, specialty coffee is still far too unknown. Now is the time to explore what the capital city of Europe has to offer. These caffeinated explorations of the city, and also the methods of preparation are unusual, fun as they are highly informative, and match a complete coffee basics course, with an extra sprinkle of fun and walking.\r\n\r\nFOR WHO\r\nThe Brussels Coffee Tours are for everyone, with a focus on the consumer\/coffee lover experience to better understand your favorite beverage! It is also suitable for HoReCa professionals who are often still unaware of what specialty coffee is, helping them to understand the poor relation of their sector but also to better understand the customer experience related to coffee. I'm here to help and hope to bridge the gap between the amateurs and the professionals. No prerequisites are necessary for this tour. Tea drinkers greatly appreciate this tour, even when they think they don't like coffee ;)\r\n\r\nOBJECTIVE\r\nThe goal of the Brussels Coffee Tours is to discover innovative places when it comes to specialty coffee, but also to discover and understand how to consume\/taste coffee based on objective quality criteria. Understanding the production chain from field to cup, the difference between specialty and commodity coffee, and learning how to better buy coffee are also central to the objectives of the Coffee Tours.\r\n\r\nDISCOVER & TASTE, AN EDUCATIONAL TOUR! - DOWNTOWN KANAAL EDITION\r\nDuring the Brussels Coffee Tours - Discover and Taste - , we wander through different areas of Brussels, depending on the edition, because traveling around specialty coffee is always a great idea to discover local trends. We will stimulate your taste buds by tasting espresso, milk drink, but also filter methods and sometimes even cold brew, nitrogen infused or not, all at my expense. You don't pay any extra for your drinks. During this DOWNTOWN KANAAL edition, we visit 4 to 5 places in the beautiful Monnaie\/Dansaert area, including a mini tasting of different fermentation processes of coffee beans. We will make you aware of the different coffee professions and discuss various topics such as: the differences in philosophies and the new waves, preparation methods, consumption habits, the barista's job, the science behind milk, sugar, taste, quality, specialty coffee, labels, roasting styles, recipes etc... but also the information to decipher on the coffee bags in order to buy better and thwart global marketing.\r\n\r\nGOOD TO KNOW\r\nThe tours always take place outdoors. We walk from one place to another and have a look at the places, but the groups being large compared to the capacity of the places, we do not consume sitting inside. It is best to bring comfortable shoes, WARM clothes in winter (better too many layers than not enough!!) and an umbrella in case of rain. Water is always recommended as well. Mask and gel in Covid times.\r\n\r\nHave breakfast beforehand because we don't have time to eat during the tours. Pssst, join us: INSTA @ok_coffee_tips\r\n\r\nYOUR HOST \r\nThomas Wyngaard is the founder of OK Coffee and one of the few Specialty Coffee experts in French-speaking Belgium. He is an independent consultant, teacher (certified by the Specialty Coffee Association from January 2018 to April 2021), tour-ist and broadcaster. After training in France, Poland and Estonia, he worked with the best in Belgium, and then migrated for almost 2 years to New York where he served as a consultant and trainer. In addition to training in the coffee business, he collaborates with Belgian roasters committed to the recognition of specialty coffee, working towards a better world \"one bean at a time\".","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/en\/detail\/id\/518572.html"},"de":{"name":"DISCOVER & TASTE Coffee Tour - Downtown Kanaal, Brussels","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/de\/detail\/id\/518572.html"},"it":{"name":"DISCOVER & TASTE Coffee Tour - Downtown Kanaal, Brussels","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/it\/detail\/id\/518572.html"},"sp":{"name":"DISCOVER & TASTE Coffee Tour - Downtown Kanaal, Brussels","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone